1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,895
A dialer profile decides how the calls of an outbound campaign are placed,

2
00:00:05,895 --> 00:00:10,240
which number customers see, and which rules every call must pass.

3
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:14,646
This video shows why it exists, the four dialing modes, and how to

4
00:00:14,646 --> 00:00:16,910
create a profile, card by card.

5
00:00:21,510 --> 00:00:25,029
An outbound campaign is a list of people to call.

6
00:00:25,029 --> 00:00:28,164
Someone has to decide how each call starts.

7
00:00:28,164 --> 00:00:33,730
Does an agent review the record and press dial, or does the system dial for them?

8
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:37,015
Every call also has to follow rules.

9
00:00:37,015 --> 00:00:39,187
Which number do customers see?

10
00:00:39,187 --> 00:00:41,058
Who must never be called?

11
00:00:41,058 --> 00:00:43,050
At what hours may you call?

12
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:47,798
Those answers should not be typed again for every list you load, and

13
00:00:47,798 --> 00:00:50,230
they should be the same for every call.

14
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:53,794
A dialer profile keeps them in one place.

15
00:00:53,794 --> 00:00:57,505
You pick a profile when you load a list of calls, so one

16
00:00:57,505 --> 00:00:59,840
profile can serve many campaigns.

17
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,777
In Preview, the agent is in control.

18
00:01:06,777 --> 00:01:11,535
The record is offered to an agent who is signed in to the campaign.

19
00:01:11,535 --> 00:01:15,510
The agent reviews it, then clicks Dial, or clicks Skip.

20
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:18,291
In Power, the system dials.

21
00:01:18,291 --> 00:01:22,783
As soon as an agent in the campaign is available, the dialer places

22
00:01:22,783 --> 00:01:25,614
calls, each with its own reserved agent.

23
00:01:25,614 --> 00:01:30,230
The record opens when the call starts, and there is nothing to press.

24
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:33,129
Progressive works like Power.

25
00:01:33,129 --> 00:01:37,304
It reserves one agent for each call, with a fixed limit on the

26
00:01:37,304 --> 00:01:39,760
calls placed in each pacing cycle.

27
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:44,592
Predictive also reserves an agent for each call by default.

28
00:01:44,592 --> 00:01:48,925
As the abandonment rate nears its limit, it places fewer calls.

29
00:01:48,925 --> 00:01:52,630
It can also over-dial, which the next video explains.

30
00:01:56,858 --> 00:01:59,831
Dialer profiles come from two features.

31
00:01:59,831 --> 00:02:03,994
Contact Center Outbound Dialer gives you Preview dialing.

32
00:02:03,994 --> 00:02:08,883
Contact Center Paced Dialing adds Power, Progressive and Predictive.

33
00:02:08,883 --> 00:02:12,318
Without it, those three modes are not offered.

34
00:02:12,779 --> 00:02:16,643
Open Interaction Center, Management, Dialer Profiles.

35
00:02:16,643 --> 00:02:20,310
The list is empty until you add the first profile.

36
00:02:20,310 --> 00:02:24,109
Older profiles saved as Manual are shown as Preview.

37
00:02:24,577 --> 00:02:26,619
Click Add Dialer Profile.

38
00:02:26,619 --> 00:02:28,726
The form is made of cards:

39
00:02:28,726 --> 00:02:35,377
General, Dialing, Caller ID, Compliance, and two more that appear only for the automatic modes.

40
00:02:39,596 --> 00:02:43,276
On General, enter a Name, and an optional Description.

41
00:02:43,276 --> 00:02:44,932
Leave Enabled ticked.

42
00:02:44,932 --> 00:02:49,654
A disabled profile places no calls, and the records loaded under it are

43
00:02:49,654 --> 00:02:52,966
not offered to agents until you turn it back on.

44
00:02:53,430 --> 00:02:56,114
On Dialing, Mode decides the pacing.

45
00:02:56,114 --> 00:02:58,286
Preview is the first choice.

46
00:02:58,286 --> 00:03:04,293
The Voice call provider is Default provider, which means the default telephony provider.

47
00:03:04,293 --> 00:03:08,000
Pick another one only when this profile must use it.

48
00:03:08,546 --> 00:03:10,832
Choose Power, and the card grows.

49
00:03:10,832 --> 00:03:15,053
Calls per agent is how many calls start each time the dialer looks

50
00:03:15,053 --> 00:03:17,456
at the campaign, from one to three.

51
00:03:17,456 --> 00:03:21,735
Each call reserves its own agent, so it never dials more calls than

52
00:03:21,735 --> 00:03:23,376
there are free agents.

53
00:03:23,855 --> 00:03:28,653
Max attempts is how many times one contact may be tried, counting the

54
00:03:28,653 --> 00:03:31,021
first call and every follow-up.

55
00:03:31,021 --> 00:03:34,795
Retry delay is the wait between attempts, in minutes.

56
00:03:34,795 --> 00:03:40,105
The subject flow can set its own rules first, and these two are the fallback.

57
00:03:40,575 --> 00:03:44,663
Ring time is how long a call rings before it is given up,

58
00:03:44,663 --> 00:03:46,545
from 15 to 120 seconds.

59
00:03:46,545 --> 00:03:52,255
Screen out answering machines can be Off, Standard detection or Premium detection.

60
00:03:52,255 --> 00:03:56,148
A machine is hung up on, and the agent never hears it.

61
00:03:56,148 --> 00:03:58,355
This works with Telnyx only.

62
00:03:58,851 --> 00:04:04,022
Show each dial to the agent decides what the agent sees while the dialer works.

63
00:04:04,022 --> 00:04:08,159
Turned on, the screen shows who is being dialed and each step.

64
00:04:08,159 --> 00:04:12,601
Turned off, it only says the agent is waiting for a connected call.

65
00:04:13,055 --> 00:04:16,039
On Caller ID, pick the number customers see.

66
00:04:16,039 --> 00:04:20,993
The list comes from your Omnichannel Addresses that are used for voice calls.

67
00:04:20,993 --> 00:04:24,455
Provider default uses the caller ID of the provider.

68
00:04:24,915 --> 00:04:29,057
A Dial from number picked when you load activities is shown instead, for

69
00:04:29,057 --> 00:04:30,597
the calls of that load.

70
00:04:30,597 --> 00:04:34,527
Tick Always show this caller ID to keep this number, even for agents

71
00:04:34,527 --> 00:04:36,385
who have a line of their own.

72
00:04:36,839 --> 00:04:41,214
Default calling region is the country assumed for a number that is written

73
00:04:41,214 --> 00:04:44,714
without a country code, which is common in imported lists.

74
00:04:44,714 --> 00:04:48,707
A number that still cannot be read is skipped, because it cannot be

75
00:04:48,707 --> 00:04:50,949
checked against a do-not-call list.

76
00:04:51,403 --> 00:04:57,297
On Compliance, Respect do-not-call and communication preferences is ticked by default.

77
00:04:57,297 --> 00:05:03,383
It skips contacts who opted out of calls, and numbers on a national do-not-call registry.

78
00:05:03,847 --> 00:05:08,305
Enforce a calling window dials only while a calendar is open, checked in

79
00:05:08,305 --> 00:05:10,305
the time zone of the contact.

80
00:05:10,305 --> 00:05:14,077
Pick the Outbound calling calendar from your business hours.

81
00:05:14,077 --> 00:05:16,877
It is required once the window is enforced.

82
00:05:17,333 --> 00:05:23,015
Power, Progressive and Predictive profiles also have an Abandoned calls card, and Predictive

83
00:05:23,015 --> 00:05:25,624
profiles have a Predictive pacing card.

84
00:05:25,624 --> 00:05:27,943
The next video walks through both.

85
00:05:28,398 --> 00:05:29,347
Click Save.

86
00:05:29,347 --> 00:05:33,142
The profile appears in the list with its mode, and it is ready

87
00:05:33,142 --> 00:05:35,598
to be picked when you load activities.

88
00:05:39,798 --> 00:05:42,276
Start with Preview for a new team.

89
00:05:42,276 --> 00:05:47,048
Agents see every record before the call, so it is the easiest to train.

90
00:05:47,798 --> 00:05:52,414
Move to Power or Progressive when agents are comfortable and the list is

91
00:05:52,414 --> 00:05:55,018
steady, so no one waits between calls.

92
00:05:55,768 --> 00:06:01,288
Keep one profile for each campaign when its abandonment rate must be measured on its own.

93
00:06:02,038 --> 00:06:05,828
Turn Enabled off to pause every load that uses a profile, then turn

94
00:06:05,828 --> 00:06:07,698
it back on when you are ready.

95
00:06:09,698 --> 00:06:14,179
A dialer profile sets the mode, the caller ID and the compliance rules

96
00:06:14,179 --> 00:06:17,305
once, and every campaign you load can reuse it.

97
00:06:17,305 --> 00:06:18,838
Thanks for watching.

